  skos:changeNote "0.3.0 (2026-10-20): Sales processes (D24): a sales service is enabled by one or more sales processes (core:supports), each built from selling steps (core:hasStep). New Sales process branch (census collection, employment cost analysis, benefits plan analysis), the census request, census validation and current benefits collection steps, and the census template, census validation report and current benefits report records. A selling step is a step of any process, and a sales service must be enabled by a process. The bridge from selling steps to the buyer persona's job steps (core:addresses) moves to the value map, a separate assembly. Built by build_domains.py from spec_sales.py against Baseline Core v1.0 (core 0.1.0)."@en ,
      "0.4.0 (2026-10-21): Restructured to the operational areas and the naming standard (D26, D27): titled 'Domain Sales Vocabulary', '… Taxonomy', '… Ontology' and '… Shapes'; imports the Commercial Operations ontology at its new IRI. Built by build_domains.py from spec_sales.py against Baseline Core v1.0 (core 0.1.0)."@en ,
      "0.1.0 (2026-10-20): first release. Built by build_domains.py from spec_sales.py against Baseline Core v1.0 (core 0.1.0)."@en ,
      "0.2.0 (2026-10-20): Sales services: the Sales service class and taxonomy branch, and the step and record kinds the first service graphs are assembled from (total cost of employment analysis, benefits comparison). Domain ontologies and shapes now name the plain ontology IRIs in owl:imports, so the KE Workbench resolves them, and pin the version built against in dcterms:requires. Built by build_domains.py from spec_sales.py against Baseline Core v1.0 (core 0.1.0)."@en ;
  owl:versionInfo "0.4.0" ;
